(in-ns 'go.arbace.waidriver) (go/file "w2g.go" :imports [

    ;; waidriver w2g OUTDIR [--stats FILE] [--chunk BYTES] MODULE...|@LIST  (doc/wasm/WAI.md §9; WA7): the modules translated by w2g
    ;; into Go packages OUTDIR/pN (package pN, which dot-imports arbace/wai), each about BYTES of Go (default 1.5 MB: a package is one
    ;; compilation of Go's, whose memory grows with it), each registering its functions by their module's SHA-256 in its init, and
    ;; OUTDIR/imports.go, the blank imports of the packages for the AOT program's main (package main, the import path
    ;; arbace/w2gout/pN). A module named twice is translated once; a module wai's validator or decoder refuses is left (the AOT
    ;; program refuses it as the driver does). STATS: a line a module, FILE<tab>FUNCS<tab>TRANSLATED<tab>LEFT (reason=count,...)
    ;; (--shared: <tab>NEW, the shapes the module added).
    ;;
    ;; --shared (WAS40 (c), WAS50 (a)): each function translated by its shape (wai.W2GShape: the immediates read from the code), each
    ;; shape written once across all the modules and registered by its key (wai.RegisterShapes), so one AOT program serves every
    ;; module whose functions' shapes it holds (a corpus's Go programs, their runtime and libraries translated once); two functions of
    ;; one key whose Go differs are an error (the key's check; --verify writes every function's Go to check it, else a shape met
    ;; again is known by its key alone).


